# Portfolio how-to-run

Whenever you change how **python-portfolio** is started, installed, tested, or which port/URLs it uses, update `HOW_TO_RUN.md` in the same change.

That file is the user’s launch guide (Command Prompt, PowerShell, and Visual Studio Code). Do not leave it stale. Do not remove it. Prefer editing it over putting launch-only instructions only in chat.

Update it when any of these change:

- `app.py` host/port or start command
- virtualenv or `requirements.txt` install steps
- `.env` / environment variable names needed to run locally
- live tool URLs under `/apps/` (add, remove, or rename a tool)
- `/api/health` or `/api/projects`
- first-time vs every-day commands
- VS Code interpreter / terminal steps
- how tests are run (`python -m pytest tests`)

Keep Command Prompt (`activate.bat`) and PowerShell/VS Code (`Activate.ps1`) commands in that file.

InvoiceFlow launch docs stay in `invoiceflow/HOW_TO_RUN.md` (port 5001). Do not mix those commands into the portfolio file unless you also note they are a separate app.
